# Tokens

- `packages/tokens/theme.css` holds exactly the shadcn token set (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--card`, …, `--chart-1..5`, `--sidebar-*`, `--radius`, `--font-sans`) as `hsl(H S% L%)`, light in `:root, [data-theme="light"]`, dark in `.dark, [data-theme="dark"]`. It is generated by `bun run tokens` from `fixtures/tokens/mapping.json` — edit the mapping, never the CSS.
- Corners: `--radius` (40px) is the one corner token of codegen 2.0 and lives in `@theme`, so plain `rounded` reads it; controls (h-8..h-14) clamp it to a pill, outer cards and bands show 40px. Nested surfaces and fields follow the nested radius rule (inner R = outer R − padding) through `rounded-nested` / `rounded-field`, dense tables use `rounded-dense`: see `radius.mdc`. Use `rounded-full` only for circles (dots, icon badges, avatars).
- `theme.css` also carries the non-color scale the blocks need (`--text-display`, `--container-page`), so packages compile in any app; `bun run check` builds `packages/adapter/test/standalone.css` (tokens + adapter only) to prove it.
- Packages (`packages/**`) use only shadcn token utilities (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, …). Never palette colors (`bg-orange-500`), never hex/rgb, never `--brand-*`.
- Tokens without a shadcn role (`--brand-orange`, `--brand-pink`, …) live only in `apps/<app>/…/brand.css` and may be used only in app CSS. `bun run check` greps `packages/` for brand tokens.
- A skin changes variable values only; markup and class names never change.
